# Testnet wallet seeds. These control real tNIGHT and tDUST; committing
# one hands its funds to anyone who reads the repo.
.seed.*

# Build output: proving keys, verifier keys, zkIR. Large, machine-specific,
# and reproducible with `npm run build`.
managed/

node_modules/

# The encrypted private-state store midnight-js keeps on disk. Holder
# secrets live here, and it is per-machine state rather than source. The
# directory name is the library's own default, from
# midnight-js-level-private-state-provider (MN_LDB_DEFAULT_DB_NAME).
.private-state/
midnight-level-db/

# deployments/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Those files are the evidence
# that something was deployed, and the web UI treats them as the only such
# evidence, so they belong in the repository.

# Serialized wallet state, so a restart does not rescan the chain. Derived
# entirely from public chain data and holds no keys -- but it does reveal
# which coins are this wallet's, so it stays out of the repository.
.wallet-cache.*.json

# Holder wallets for the on-chain demo. These are SECRETS: whoever has one
# can present that credential. Persisted because losing one strands its
# leaf on chain forever -- unpresentable and unrevocable.
.holders.*.json
